## Why This Is Asked
Tests programmatic planning and cross‑team coordination for a high‑risk migration that must preserve reliability while delivering features. It also probes governance, risk controls, and measurable progress.

## Key Concepts
- Phased migration with canary and blue/green patterns
- Cross‑team ownership: telemetry, incident management, deployment
- Acceptance criteria, Definition of Ready, gate reviews
- Reliability metrics (SLOs), rollback strategies, and feature flags

## Code Example
```javascript
// Example: canary flag check
if (featureFlags.canaryEnabled(service)) {
  routeToCanary(service);
} else {
  routeToStable(service);
}
```
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you adjust thresholds if observed latency creeps above SLO during canary?
- What governance cadences would you enforce to keep all teams aligned over 8 weeks?

## Why This Is Asked
Gauges ability to operationalize privacy across multiple squads and regions while preserving velocity, balancing governance with execution.

## Key Concepts
- Privacy-by-design and DPIA governance
- Data minimization and consent management
- CI gates and artifact templates
- Region-specific privacy budgets and rituals

## Code Example
```javascript
// Pseudo CI gate: enforce privacy checks before merge
function privacyGate(feature) {
  if (!feature.hasDPIA || !feature.consentSchemaValid) {
    throw new Error('Privacy gate failed');
  }
  return true;
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you measure fatigue or compliance drift across regions?
- What would you automate to keep DPIA upkeep lightweight for fast-moving features?
